No liberating novel for Tymoshenko through parliament
The Ukrainian parliament today refused the request, in the context of an amendment of the criminal code, to abolish those paragraphs on the basis of which opposition leader Yulia Timoshenko had been convicted.
The new regulation, which could have paved the way to the exemption of the imprisoned prime minister, was rejected by deputies at the second reading of the request for mitigating the penalties for economic offenses.
Tymoshenko was sentenced to seven years imprisonment in October over the conclusion of an allegedly detrimental contract with Russia for purchasing natural gas.
The verdict is not yet final, in December the appeal of the convicts is to be heard in court.
Tymoshenko himself calls the verdict a political revenge of the regime and also in the West the trial raised suspicions of bias of the judgment.
The request to remove paragraph 365, on the basis of which the Prime Minister was convicted, was supported by 147 deputies.
226 votes would have been required for its adoption.
Libyan Victory
The history of the Libyan liberation struggle or Libyan rebellion already knows its losers.
Muammar Gaddafi is buried in an undisclosed place in the desert and without him the war is over.
Now only the winners have to be defined.
As is customary for this region, Islamists prevail in the elections, the question is only which - the moderate or the radical.
The National Transitional Council professed itself to the customary law of Sharīʿa, of which one now has a certain notion with God.
Libyia would become a country without crime, because for the theft, in short, the hand is choked off.
Women, too, should forget thoughts of emancipation as quickly as possible, any apostates are executed, and so on.
Instead of a single dictatorator, society will be united by the Qur’an from each othe-in-command tribe in the future.
In short - there will be an order in Libya that would hardly be imaginable and, above all, hardly desirable.
Only - our lifestyle is not the only and objectively probably not the best and would hardly fit variety to the aforementioned Libyans.
From this point of view, it is rather strange that the Muslim fighters let themselves be helped by the unbelieving dogs at all.
Apologies may only be the fact that NATO's air strikes were directed not by any general from America, but by Allah himself, whose omnipotence was praised after every successful hit.
The winners in Libya? The West is not one of them.
We only participated in an exchange of gunfire, served the interests of Islam and our politicians got rid of themselves in the person of the dictator of a political ally, without bringing any advantage.
After the fresh and bad experiences from Afghanistan and Iraq, we preferred to refrain from a military occupation of Libya.
As a result, the locals are rid of a concern - namely the expulsion of the crusaders.
But do the petroleum companies get the black gold at a mocking price even without occupation?
Hardly and so the West can finally boast with its selflessness in terms of the protection of human rights.
If this does not spoil the Sharīʿa representatives for them.
Beginning of a new crisis era
France and the rest of Europe in the focus of investors.
On Tuesday, a statistical storm low roared through Europe.
The individual states published their data on their GDP for the 3rd quarter.
The Czech economy stagnated compared to the previous quarter, Germany and France increased.
Today, however, the obligation market breaks all records.
Investors are keeping an eye not only on Greece, but also Spain, France, Austria and other countries.
The statistical offices of the Europe zone, Germany, the Czech Republic and several other European countries published their preliminary forecasts on economic development in the third quarter.
As expected, Germany's GDP grew by 0.5%, that of France by 0.4%.
Both countries simultaneously corrected their data for the second quarter, in which Germany recorded higher growth than had originally been expected (growth by 0.3% instead of predicted 0.1%), while France admitted a slight decline of 0.1% (originally data only spoke of stagnation).
The Czech economy grewed by 1.5 percent year-on-year in this year's third quarter.
Compared to the previous quarter, however, gross domestic product stagnated and according to Tsch. Statistical Office thus confirmed the trend of slowing growth in economic performance.
Thus, the results are worse than the analysts' forecasts.
The most important events:
The Czech economy grewed by 1.5 percent year-on-year in this year's third quarter, but it stagnated compared with the previous quarter.
Preliminary and seasonally overcalculated data, the German economy grewed by 0.5 percent in the third quarter.
Across the eurozone and the EU, the economy recorded 0.2 per cent growth between July and September compared to the previous quarter, in line with analysts' expectations.
The Greek economy shrank 5.2 percent year-on-year.
Yields from their 10-year-old government bonds reached the value of 28.45%.
The yield on Italian and Spanish government bonds rose to their critical limits.
Austria, the Netherlands, France, Belgium and other countries are also beginning to feel problems...
The yield on Czech government bonds is below 4%, even as the situation in the region deteriorates.
In Germany, voices are heard that the ECB should become the creditor of the last instance.
The Czechs qualified for EURO
In Montenegro they won 1:0 and are now celebrating their qualifiers for 200 million
The football selection has mastered the heaviest task of the whole season!
Thanks to a well-placed goalkeeper Čech and a magnificent goal by Petr Jiráček, she won 1:0 in Montenegro.
With a large portion of luck, Czech football was able to defend its luxurious advantage from the home game and will once again not be missed at the European Championship.
IHNED.cz followed the promotion game in an in-depth reportage.
Little excitement in the first half and a giant portion of luck in the second.
The Czech selection also triumphed quite happily 1:0 thanks to the final weakness of the home team, a brilliant Čech's and the hero of the day Jiráček in Montenegro and has thus redeemed her ticket for the European Football Championship.
Also because of the precise defensive game of the Czech team, they were only able to put more pressure on the Montenegrins in the second half.
The unlucky birds of the game were Damjanovic and Vucinic, who missed two huge chances.
Also thanks to an excellent Petr Čech, the Czech selection will be involved next year at the European Championships, it is also pleasing that domestic football has a premium of about 200 million.
From the first few minutes quite combative football was played.
Both teams combined lengthily and so was mainly played around the centre line.
Even in the second half, the pressure of the home team failed and the wide tees in front of the penalty area were successfully repelled by the Czech defence.
Iranian students are willing to die for their country's core program.
They formed a living shield.
A few hundred university students formed a living sign around a core object in Iran.
With this gesture, they wanted to demonstrate their support for their country's core program before a possible Israeli attack.
The students had prayed at noon in front of the object on Tuesday and subsequently announced death to the U.S. and Israel.
A few hundred students from the university in Isfahan, Iran, formed a living shield around the core technology center in Isfahan, where uranium is being processed on Tuesday.
In doing so, they wanted to announce that they are willing to protect their country’s core program, if necessary also with their own lives.
The International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA) recently stated in its report that Iran did not appear to give up its efforts for a nuclear weapon.
There is also talk in Israel about a possible attack on Iranian nuclear facilities.
Students had prayed at noon in front of the entrance to the complex and then promulgated death to the U.S. and Israel.
In the event of an intention-maked attack to paralyze Iran's nuclear program to the greatest possible extent, according to the Israeli press from the center in Isfahan, it would also be the nuclear enrichment facility in Natan's target.
The menu of a fat-addicted child: It doesn't have breakfast and eats sausage for dinner
More than one-third of children from 9 to 13 have overweight problems, with 9 per cent of all pupils and 5 per cent of all children being overweight.
Recent surveys have been shown - obese children mostly come from families with an unhealthy lifestyle.
This demonstrates once again how important it is for a person’s healthy development of the milieu in which he grows up and are the examples that surround him.
On the tables of obese children, sausages are up to half more often on the table than in families where normal-weight children live.
More than 19 percent of the overweight children had fries on the previous day of the enlightenment campaign under the motto "Obesity is no coincidence".
In families with thickers, exercise is not one of the favorite activities, but this also affects the majority of today's students - only 15 percent replied that their parents at least once a week find time for active exercise.
survey of 900 children
The survey took place last year towards the end of the school year, during which almost 900 children from primary schools across the Czech Republic were surveyed.
This was already the second year of the campaign "Obesity is no coincidence", which is supported by the general health insurance company and the company Unilever.
So far, more than 12 thousand students from 4th and 8th grades have participated in the project.
Unhealthy diet and a lack of movement in the family are decisive factors that are responsible for the frighteningly increasing number of children with overweight or even obesity.
"Only half of the children surveyed, for example, cited eating five times a day, breakfast-second breakfast-lunch-vesper-evening bread - one of the main requirements for a healthy diet," according to one of the survey results.
No breakfast and sausage for dinner
Experts point out that even relative small things, such as the regular breakfast time of the family, are also important for the healthy development of a child.
In the Czech Republic, however, only 23 percent of the families of the students have breakfast.
And - in most families, everyone eats breakfast on their own.
Worst of all, the finding was that in every tenth family there is no breakfast at all.
Breakfast is considered the cornerstone of a healthy daily diet.
Among other things, the survey test showed that unhealthy fries are consumed much more often in the families of overweight children.
And almost everyone - regardless of weight - drinks sweet sodas every day (70 percent)
Although more than 40 percent of the children surveyed play sports, only less than half of their parents do so - only 15 percent.
Assemble your own menu
Another part of the survey allowed selected children (204 boys and 172 girls from 13 schools) to assemble their own diet from opportunities offered for appetite and opinion.
"What Czech children between 12 and 15 prefer in terms of diet is far removed from the ideal of a healthy diet.
Among their favourite dishes were many pastries, meat dishes and, of course, desserts.
"Alarming is above all the great popularity of sweet sodas," is emphasized in the final report on this survey.
At lunch, i.e. the main course, pasta won just ahead of poultry.
The children almost did not like legumes at all and the popularity of fish and vegetable dishes as lunches was also very low.
Return to Health
At the same time, however, the survey also showed that the children are quite willing to change their eating habits if they get proper information.
"In many cases, the control group of survey participants, who completed the questionnaire following the conclusion of the enlightening lecture "Obesity is not a coincidence", there was in many cases a significant shift in preferences towards the principles of healthy diet," the results of the project stated.
Obviously, this was evident, for example, with the sweet sodas, where many children began to give priority to ordinary water.
The children also ticked poultry or fish much more often in the questionnaire as the main dish of the day and were willing to eat less dumplings or sweet foods.
Professions claim - a stylist must also be a good psychologist
In the introductory article about how stylists learn, I had complained a bit that this was a bit too much stuff to get started.
I didn’t know in the slightest that came.
Lectures by three professionals from the industry, the clothing of problematic figures and a seminar about how the "on the pitch" runs.
It's supposed to get even worse.
The closer the exam approaches, the more information and practical tasks ahead of us.
But even if the course takes place every Saturday and Sunday, it is still fully occupied.
This time we debated with Director Alena (not a single man participates in the course), how to attract a woman who doesn't have an ideally proportioned figure.
After all, that’s most of us.
One has a too short neck, the others have a too young figure without decent curves and still others are chubby.
It is up to the stylist to visually conceal broad shoulders, to lengthen the neck or to conjure up the necessary curves.
We also got tips on how to put on a woman's type like Jennifer Lopez - i.e. with big bosoms, wide hips and narrow waist - pretty and figure-hugging, without looking too provocative.
If, for example, the difference between waist and hips is so great that the skirt or the pants really does not fit, you should at least have a piece tailored.
You certainly won't regret that, because well-fitting clothes are just priceless.
In such a tailor-made skirt you feel much better than in an off-the-shelf, which always slips up and slid, stands out in the waist, etc.
Boy-like figures, in turn, can allow themselves to wear clothing with pleats, bulges, appliqués, embroideries or gather.
With this amount of information and figure types, I'm happy that I have a whole week to let everything go through my mind thoroughly.
And yet I'm afraid it's almost unworkable in view of the applied home assignment.
Each of the students was assigned a celebrity, for whom she should come up with suitable outfits - daywear and evening robe.
In doing so, we are supposed to take into account the current appearance, the fashion style of the corresponding star and its figure type.
I'm supposed to "attach" Miranda Kerr that you might know from the Victoria's Secret campaign.
Insidiously, I jubile, because this is much better for me personally than, for example, attracting Britney Spears or Christina Aguilera, who has probably gained about a hundred kilos in recent times (well, that's a bit exaggerated), or the young Selena Gomez.
We are supposed to cut the garments out of magazines or search on the Internet, print them out and then edit them graphically.
In the "Moodboard", as the whole result is called, our very personal style and our relationship to graphic design should then be expressed.
It is very important to also think about the graphical side of styling.
The stylist not only attracts the models purely physically, but also designs the so-called product page in the journals (according to concrete specifications, for example, trend handbags, coats, etc.).
Stylist and designer Mario Kameník told us about this.
But it's not until Sunday.
This means that a stylist must have a good overall overview.
The Saturday lecture, filled with information about figure types, was spiced by three visitors from the industry:
the stylist Jan Pokorný, the fashion designer Jakub Polanka and the fashion photographer Ben Renč.
Jakub reminded us that fashion is an illusion and a stylist should be able to take advantage of it.
And stylistist can work with a single piece of clothing in very different ways.
The magic word is variability.
For example, you can wear a trench coat over the jeans as usual, such as a t-shirt or coat, but you can also wear it on the bare body, put heels on it and wear it as a dress.
It’s enough to roll up the sleeves or the collar and the whole look will look very different.
"Play with it," he insisted.
However, the following advice came to me the most: "First you have to know the rules perfectly."
"It's only then that you're allowed to hurt her," Jakub said.
Finally I realize why we have to tample all these doctrines, what you can combine with what and why, even if you often get to see something completely different in fashion journals.
Not to mention fashion shows.
Thanks to photographer Ben, I now know that a stylist must have prepared many more clothing variants than he ultimately photographs.
So you have to be prepared for a fashion story with ten pages (i.e. ten outfits) to style at least fifteen.
And also that the clothing in the photo in combination with other accessories sometimes looks very different than in reality.
So you have to reckon with all this when designing the outfit.
Jan Pokorný also confirmed that image and styl sometimes account for half of the success.
You just need Madonna to look at a not exactly brilliant singer from whom image and marketing have made a world star.
In the Czech Republic, the services of a stylist are rather reserved.
Even well-known personalities often consider this to be thrown out money (the main thing is that I bring something, how I look is secondary).
And if one of us can be styled, then we should reckon that he or she will most likely impose us on a completely different (smaller) size than he or she really needs.
Then you only have to google afterwards to determine with certainty that the tabloid press writes that the corresponding celebrity has closed or decreased again, etc.
Jan and Mario urged us on Sunday not to believe that a stylist only needs to focus on fashion and then "assemble" the outfit.
In his work he has to communicate mainly with the people he styles and he must be a clever psychologist.
Assessing people without offering themselves and standing by their opinion.
"If anyone manager orders us to sift over her closet and add pretty pieces, then we can't clear the whole closet and say to her - my God, that's terrible."
"You have to find at least a few commendable things that you're recommending what you can wear," Mario says.
He also showed us quite concretely what such a so-called "place bag" must contain.
So such a bag, which you buttook at the waist and in which you carry all the necessary proprieties with you.
In addition to such clear things, such as scissors, hair-removal unwinders or safety pins, it also contains such utensils, such as a nylon thread (thus the stylist assists in photographing products, such as handbags or hats), special clips with which the clothes at the back are ruffled if it is too big (pins or other clamps are prohibited so that the fabric does not break) and
However, so that we not only have to listen, but can also try out something practically, we learned how to properly undergue shoes.
Even when photographing in the studio, where the floor is level, you can damage the shoe sole, let alone the outside.
We glued and glued...
With the scissors you must not even touch the shoes so that you do not damage them.
So you really have to proceed skillfully.
Mario delighted me by praising my "creation" without restrictions.
The mentioned skill is not exactly my strength.
All of this was only a fraction of what we heard at the second weekend sequel course.
One thing has become clear to me in the meantime - devoting to styling on a professional level is not child's play.
V Need for Speed: "The Run" - the Illegal race across America
Review
The originally careless ride is caused by a series of completely avoidable, dilettante mistakes for routine driving to the early shift.
Although it was possible to fulfill the ambitions to a large extent, but what good is that if obviously no one wanted to do a bit more.
Even before he came to the counters, the new part with the subtitle "The Run" aroused high expectations.
After all, he promised to move the game series "Need for Speed", which had already been yearned, back into a new dimension and in the playable demonstration examples he actually seemed to be not just one of many action racing games.
We were also curious about how the fitted passages turn out, in which the main protagonist gets out of the car and continues on foot.
But as you’re used to NFS, there’s a lot different in the end than you’d expected.
Surely - potentially it's quite decent arcade races, but overall the game is diminished by some superfluous errors that are more or less already present in this series for a few years.
So it is actually no longer mistakes, but rather signs of a basically incomprehensible laziness of the game developers.
The adventure starts very well.
For the first time you will be introduced to the story, whose main character Jack has certain problems of personal character; the only solution seems to be to participate in an illegal race across America.
In San Francisco, so on the west coast, you sit on the steering wheel - with the task of being the first in New York.
The basic idea contains a number of interesting elements.
The entire route is divided into ten stages and more than fifty individual races.
This means that each race is held on a different track and that the individual stages take place in different, sufficiently different and interesting environments.
You don't have the impression for a moment that game would offer the same thing again and again.
Some environments are also very pretty to look at, although the technical level of the graphics does not go beyond that of the earlier parts of the series.
So nothing world-moving.
But the drive through the desert, through autumnal landscape or high up through snow-covered screedy landscape looks visually very pleasant.
From time to time, atypical elements bring a little variety into the individual races.
In the desert, for example, one is surprised by a desert storm that severely restricts visibility.
In the mountains, in turn, you have to be careful not to be buried by an avalanche.
By the way, the individual races are quite well installed in succession.
Only a few, but they're enough.
For a while you try to overtake the prescribed number of opponents (in principle a classic race), then you have time to catch up (classical race against the stopwatch), then a personal duel with a single opponent awaits you.
And this also interferes with the police, who want to screw up the whole thing.
One novelty are passages in which Jack leaves the car.
It’s more about certain interactive animations in which Jack flees from someone and where the player has to help him by pressing the right button at the right moment.
So nothing complicated.
It is surprising, however, that there are much fewer such passages in the game than you would expect (in particular probably only three).
Ultimately, this is rather beneficial to the matter, because at least this element has no chance of becoming boring - it belongs in the context of the above to the elements that make the game more varied.
The driving model follows in the footsteps of the preceding parts.
That is, seen from today’s point of view, it does not tear out trees, on the other hand, one could not claim that it would be bad.
If you’re looking for realistic simulations, you have to look elsewhere.
But an action-packed racing, the local driving model continues to do justice quite well, even though you could find betters with the competition.
Until then, everything is in the best order.
Real problems only arise after some time.
In contrast to the driving model, the collision model is not quite O.K.
From a game of this kind it is hardly to be expected to calculate complicated deformations and collisions, but if you practically do not have any impact on any object how the car behaves, then obviously not everything is okay.
Typical example: In some places you "streak" the other car only slightly, but in other, almost identical situation, you get into skidding and turn wild pirouettes.
Or does the cart go straight to junk.
Thanks to the restart system, this does nothiness anymore, it's always annoying.
The restarts are solved in this way: if you have total damage or land far away from the track, then the game throws you back to the last clue of the track.
Only - in every race you only have five restarts.
If you have exhausted them, everything starts from the beginning.
The restarts are therefore rather something like an aid, in the event that something does not succeed, but you should not rely on it.
Sometimes, however, the restart doesn’t even help, so nothing helps but to learn the critical section out of your head.
It’s extremely unpleasant that the same things often happen in the same places.
Some curves, for example, you have to drive through in a very specific way, otherwise you just don't fit through.
Elsewhere, in the appropriate place "civilic" cars are always encountered in the same configuration, regardless of whether you come first or fifth, five seconds sooner or a minute later.
This is especially annoying in situations when you see that the opponent passes two oncoming cars in front of you, but until you get there, the cars are already in such a position that you have to drive or brake them.
And it doesn’t matter when you get there, because everything is designed in such a way that this situation always comes close to your nose.
Opponents have other advantages.
In the whole game there are a few places where you are always overtaken in the same place by the same opponent and here again without regard to the time.
This is most crazy at the conclusion of the game on the long bridge, which one passes in the opposite direction.
The opponent obviously has to overtake one here on devil come out.
And if he's in front of one, he'll of course take your sight, so you drive your own car a few times in Klump.
Sure - you just want to make the game more exciting and exciting, but this intention is so clear that it quickly gives you the pleasure of the game.
And that’s a pity, because despite a simpler driving model, the game is quite entertaining overall and in some places so action-packed that you almost don’t know where your head stands anymore.
And in principle it doesn't matter what's "to blame" - the concept with fifty unique routes, the arrangement of the races in a way that no boredom can arise, or something completely different...
An unusual idea is also the change of car in the course of the races.
You must not overlook the petrol stations on the route, because especially here you can change the car, although in most cases the car that you currently have is sufficient.
Cars are divided into three categories.
The sports cars are well suited for the urban areas, the strong American limousines for the straight highways and exotic super sports cars for the technical rides, for example on the serpentines in the mountains.
Hand-in-hand with the mode of game history also goes the task mode (challenges) - i.e. the races in the individual localities you know from history.
Here there are not only medals, but also experience points for your own profile, which is together for the tasks (challenges) and the history.
In order to get to the higher driver level, various objects must be unlocked: starting from the car to the backgrounds for the profile.
This is also associated with the online autolog function, which, among other things, compares its own achieved results with those of other players and also ensures further collective functions.
One more incomprehensible snatcher is a situation in the final race in history.
Here you come by car into a subway tunnel (my reasons), where you race in the dark on the rails (because of me).
On the speedometer there are digits between 150 a 200 km/h (my reasons), but suddenly a subway arrives from behind and drives you uncompromisingly to scrap.
In our editors, we will probably argue for a long time about whether this was a blackout of the game designers or whether the authors consider us so stupid.
The technical side is nothing overwhelming but at least the overall visual impression is quite appealing in most cases and even brilliant here and there.
It is all the more annoying that at some exciting moments the refresh rate becomes slower and sometimes quite dramatic.
However, this applies in particular to accidents with a larger number of participants, where a continuous FPS is of no use anyway.
The tone reproduction is so far O.K. and the soundtrack is a matter of taste.
In an effort to appeal to young audiences as broad as possible scale, a soundtrack a lá "from everyone something" was created - but who buys such a game because of the music?!
Need for Speed: The Run? The feelings are rather mixed.
If the game wasn't diminished by the totally unnecessary mistakes mentioned, we could've argued with the chest tone of conviction that The Run is the best piece by NFS in recent years.
But that's how the game somehow seems unfinished.
A great pleasure in itself, but you should be prepared to have these mistakes stake into your eyes with the power of airport headlights.
Concert of the "Students of the velvety revolution" with singing ensembles of Charlemagne University
For the third time, the Festival Festa Academica offers the combination of World Student Day with the anniversary of the Velvet Revolution, including a musical experience.
In the course of the festive, the twenty specialist and university choirs introduce themselves.
The focus of the festival is on the two concerts, which take place on 17 November.
"Charlemagne University has a large share in the festival."
"Among the participants is also represented by the choir of the Faculty of Education and the Faculty of Humanistic Studies and on the festival committee also sits the Rector Václav Hampl," the head of the organizing team, Jakub Čaloun.
The absolute highlight of the festival is the public concert of technical school choirs, which takes place on 17 November from 2 p.m. on the square in front of the National Technical Library in Dejvice.
On the program is the composition of the eminent Czech jazzer Karel Růžička "Celebration Jazz Mass".
In the evening hours, in the gala rooms of the Volkshaus in Vinohrady, the concert "Studenty sametu" (Studenty sametu), in which university choirs also perform, choirs of Charles University are not excluded.
Festa Academica aims not only to celebrate World Student Day and commemorate the 22nd anniversary of the Veld Revolution, but to present choral music to the public at the highest level and to promote the creative cooperation of young people.
The main organizer is the Association of Czech Choirs in cooperation with the Johannes-Kepler-Gymnasium.
Bohuslav Svoboda, the Lord Mayor of the capital Prague and Václav Hampl, the rector of Charles University, took over the patronage of the entire event.
The festival will take place from 16 to 20 November in Prague and Pardubice.
In addition to festive concerts, the schedule also includes numerous music meetings, student happanings, matinees and other events.
Interested parties can find detailed information on the websites of the festival www.festaacademica.cz
EU Ambassador Vicenová:
The Czechans have the reputation of negativists and Eurosceptics
"The Treaty of Lisbon has put the balamon among the individual institutions palpably out of hand."
“I didn’t expect such a tough war.”
"It will be five or six years before the waves are smoothed and everyone will get used to their new role," Milena Vicenová, the Czech ambassador to the European Union, began her lecture quite sharply at the Faculty of Law.
In the first part of her lecture, she showed how seriously she takes the motto "Understandably and openly about Europe", in which she succeeded in describing the individual organs of the EU and their mutual relations in such a manageable and understandable way that it could have envied some of the lectors of the Faculty of Law of Charles University.
Ms Vicenová also praised the new permanent chairman of the Council of Europe Herman Van Rompuy:
"Initially, there was criticism that he was too inconspicuous - a grey official who could not cope with such a role, but I have to say it took everyone's breath at how well he took care of the matter.
“He is a person who manages to listen patiently to twenty-seven member states, to communicate with them and above all to have clear ideas about how to proceed with the EU.
In response to the answer to the question: who is this – the European Union? What number should I call?’ as an important step towards the unification and better readability of EU policy towards countries, such as China or India.
No one wants to ban us our oilkeeper quargel
Ms Vicenová also devoted herself to the agenda according to which the European Union lived, lives and commemorated living in the near future.
She described the Czech presidency two years ago as a success.
The Czechs had mastered the financial crisis and the gas crisis and also organized the summit meeting for Eastern Partnership.
She described the fall of the government during the presidency as a major negative, which severely harmed the image of the Czech Republic.
Czech Representation in the EU currently has its hands full.
In the words of the ambassador, it was not only the chairmanship, but also in the subsequent crisis, which has not yet been overcome, quite hectic.
And that’s where the EU’s seven-year budget has yet to be endorsed, making things much more complicated precisely because of today’s economic situation.
Whether it will be a sleek and frugal budget, which economic sectors take precedence, which countries will be promoted more and which are less - all this is now on the agenda.
The ambassador also reminiscent of her own slogans, with whom she came to Brussels: "Understandably about Europe."
"If I don't like something, it's greyish abbreviations, foreign words and technical jargon that no one understands.
How can I, as a citizen, actually know whether you are really crooked in Brussels or thinking round cucumbers and bananas of different sizes, or if someone actually wants to ban us from quargel.
It would also have liked to use the soil of the EU to get more Czechs into European institutions.
Europe of two or different rates in prospect
According to the EU ambassador, the Czechs have a reputation for being Eurosceptics, who perceive more the negative than the positive aspects of the matter.
All the more annoying is the weak representation of Czechs in European institutions.
Many factors are to blame for this, including the restraint of our candidates, their inability to write motivation letters and, last but not least, the weak support of the Czech side.
In addition to the successful Czech Presidency, she also emphasized the strength and cooperation of the Visegrad Group, the so-called V4.
"Believe me, if a Pole or Hungarian comes to me and there's a Slovak nearby, then the Frenchman next to me means: "Hey, what are your heads together - is that your V4 again?"
According to Vicenové, the EU expects hard rules for the budget policies of the member states in the future.
As much realer, as a "European federation," she sees the concept of one Europe of two or even different speeds.
"We have here the countries of the eurozone and the countries away from the eurozone.
"We have the Schengen area and we already have the institute of strengthened cooperation."
"For the first time, it has been said that only the countries that want it and those who don't want it are supposed to stand quietly off."
"There will be more and more such institutions, which ultimately amounts to a strong "Europe of different speeds," Ms Vicenová expects.
In this regard, it also acknowledged the role of the Czech Republic and Herman Van Rompuyes in enforcing the principle, according to which all issues with an impact on the entire EU must be discussed by all member states and not only by eurozone countries.
Brand Story:
Innovator IBM enters the second-century of its existence
If you wanted to look for a suitable word that characterizes IBM's strategy most accurately, this would probably be the word "longevity".
For the general public, IBM is synonymous with technological revolution, known as a modern company, even though a century has elapsed since its inception.
The basis for this longevity has already been laid by their first boss - the visitor Thomas J. Watson sen.
He already represented the slogan, countless worldwide problems could be easily solved if people were willing to think a bit.
His slogan "Think!" thus became a hallmark, around which the life of the future giant should take place (and at the same time as the title of the company-internal magazine, which was started to be published by IBM in 1935).
This was also the basis of Watsen's thoroughly prepared corporate culture.
"For us from IBM, this long-term thinking means a continual movement towards the future.
IMB survived and was also successful for a whole century because it has remained true to its principles and did not shy away from changing everything else all around.
This allowed us, over the course of our first century, to transform technologies, business and society.
We hope that we will create even more in the next hundred years," said Samuel J. Palmisano, the company's current director on the occasion of the anniversary.
Conceived system
As early as the thirties, Watson pursued the social care of his employees - in a similar way, as entrepreneur Baťa in Czechoslovakia: IBM people were one of America's first employees to have paid leave, insurance by the entrepreneur plus elegant uniforms as workwear and a well-thought-out remuneration system for best newers and traders.
IBM's long-term relationships with its customers are just as sophisticated, too.
From the beginning, the company has been ingenious in talent promotion - as one of the first companies in the world, IBM overturned any discrimination - and was able to choose accordingly.
In line with this anti-discrimination strategy is also the current plan Palmisan, at the helm of IBM next year, will also be alternated by a woman - by Virginia Rometty.
She has been with IBM for thirty years, so far she took the position of sales, marketing and strategy chief.
In recent years, IBM has done so-called online brainstorming, from which many future strategies and innovations arise.
No wonder - there are enough ideas, almost half a million people are employed in the company.
An institution with a good reputation
Their unwavering position in the business guarantees the company a strong image and this both internally and externally.
"From the beginning, IBM had the concept of an institution rather than a mere technology company," Economist told Harvard Business School professor and author of a book about IBM, Rosabeth Moss Kanter.
"IBM isn't a technology company, it's a company that helps solve business problems using technologies," added George Colony of consulting firm Forrester Research.
As the companient itself emphasizes, it’s a difference to only be present in the market or form it directly through this presence.
IBM - in the states of their logos due to "Big Blue," has grown into one of the world's largest companies in a century.
It’s one of the most versatile technology companies ever—IBM develops hardware and software, infrastructures, hosting, and consulting services in an incredible range of products—from servers to nanotechnology.
Of all American technology companies, IBM owns the most patents and five of its employees have already been awarded the Nobel Prize.
His best-known inventions include, e.g. ATMs, credit cards, financial swaps, barcode or even the floppy.
With about 220 billion dollars stock market value (market capitalization), IBM was the second-largest technology company this year (equally after Apple), overtaking Microsoft for the first time since 1996.
The look ahead
Not all products and innovations met the tastes of today's customers - unfortunate were, for example, the attempt with their own operating system OS/2, the online service Prodigy or the computers IBM PC jr.
"Business is based on the forward movement, so you can't bind yourself emotionally to the past," says Samuel J. Palmisano.
That's why IBM has no quite a buoy of building its foundations on different platforms - and if they don't work, leaving them again.
In contrast to the opponent Microsoft, which in principle stands and falls with its Windows operating system.
Promising technologies
IBM’s profits are largely attended by services, software and hardware contribute to one-fifth each.
In 1990, hardware with a more than fifty percent share was the most heavily represented.
Since 2000, IMB has divested low-income assets worth 15 billion dollars, but in the same time it invested 58 billion dollars in the purchase of promising technologies.
In these investments, IBM continues even after 2008, when the modern financial crisis swept over the world for the first time like a storm.
Here, too, IBM remained true to the legacy of its first boss, Thomas J. Watson, who increased his level of investment in the midst of the great global economic crisis.
So far, it seems that the company IBM survives today's crisis unscathed.
The value of IBM shares has risen 120 per cent rocket-like since 2008 and the company's net profit is growing continually.
IBM's corporate slogan reads: everything can be changed - only the values don't.
For this reason, too, it can be expected that this flexible giant will also cope with the next crisis.
IBM history: From cheese cutter to spaceflight
Founded one hundred years ago in New York, IBM (International Business Machines) initially had a rather complicated name - Computing Tabulating Recording Corporation.
She took over the name IBM only in 1924 - originally it was a brand name for a subsidiary in Canada and South America.
The foundation for the later company IBM was laid by the merger of four companies, whose history dates back to the 80s of the 19th century.
They possessed technologies such as the famous puncture card clocks to register the start and end of work.
Charles Ranlett Flint became the architect of this new company, who also held the chairmanship of the supervisory board until 1930.
And it was Flint, who hired the boss of the competitor company Thomas J. Watson, so that he helped him with the management of the company.
This leader eclipsed even the founders of IBM - Watson's ideas are still based on the invincible culture and identity of the company to this day.
Watson headed the company until 1952.
IBM, as the name suggests, began with the production and distribution of all possible machines for the trade - from sausage and cheese cutters to checkouts.
In the first four decades in which Watson led the company, he doubled its revenues to nine million dollars and the company gradually expanded to all continents.
Watson was so indispensable for the company that he sat in the executive chair for forty years, only then he was replaced by his son, Thomas Watson Junior.
Under his leadership, IBM began to work on the development of artificial intelligence and also developed the first programming language.
In the '60s technicians and computers from IBM helped NASA conduct flights into space - to Mercury and Saturn, and in 1996, man's famous flight to the moon.
Meanwhile, in 1964 IBM developed the first computer family with the same computer architecture - the IBM System/360 series.
A classic PC, which determined the computer standard of that time, came on the market in 1981 under the name IBM 5150.
Twenty years later, IBM sold its computer production to the Chinese company Lenovo, but on the other hand it bought the consultant part of PricewaterhouseCoopers and thus fully entered the business with consulting services and services with high added value.
The strategy IBM pays off over the past three years is the "Smarter Planet" concept.
It embodies the intention to use technologies wisely in areas not previously planned, e.g. also to improve the situation in transport and city administration.
In the retail sector, IBM recently introduced the "smarter commerce" platform, which is intended to help merchants lead the entire commercial cycle.
IBM also has a strong history in the Czech Republic.
As early as 1923, IBM founded a branch office in Czechoslovakia at that time - as the first country ever in Central and Eastern Europe.
Today IBM ČR also operates a strategic outsourcing center in Brno.
The headquarters for Central and Eastern Europe is located in Prague and there is also a top team of world-class researchers dealing with voice recognition technology.
Darina Rychtářová about her unfaithful husband:
Iveta - You can keep this donkey, I don't want it anymore!
Darina Rychtářová (53) says - now it's over!
After her husband Josef Rychtář (53) had become their lover by the protector of Iveta Bartošová (45), Darina still had the hope that Joseph would wake up from his pink dream and come home.
But now it's finally over with the patience and for the further life she has set clear rules.
"Joseph can come home, but nothing more than my partner," explained D. Rychtářová.
When Darina RychtÙová had offered refuge to the singer I Bartošová in her own house, she probably wouldn’t have dreamed how this would turn out with her husband.
When Iveta moved out and back to Říčany after 30 days at her insistence, Joseph immediately went along.
He even publicly confessed that he loved her.
In that time, Darina resigned, yes it even seemed as if she wanted to reconcile with her unfaithful husband - but now she finally gave him the running pass.
Rychytář doesn't care who his wife sleeps with
If Rychtář Iveta Bartošová were to leave in the future, he would certainly not receive open arms at home.
"He is the biological father of my dreams, and if he wants to decide his days in our common home, then I won't chase him out."
"However, not as a loved old donkey, but as a person to whom I still have certain bonds," Ms. Rychtářová revealed; but she also said that she had already emotionally separated from him and insisted solely on mutual decency.
The circumstance that Darina has locked his back door so far carries Josef with dignity.
“I respect my wife’s decision.”
"I'm sticking with Iveta, that doesn't change."
"My wife wants paper marriage, and that's what I respect."
"The company keeps running, I'll take care of the repairs, the garden, the property, I'll do the purchases."
"With Darina, I'm talking normally, but we don't share the bed," said J. Rychtář (the paper) Blesk.
If Darina wants to look for a new love, he doesn’t want to prevent it.
"We don't sleep with each other, so I don't care if she has a boyfriend or who that's.
I realize it's my fault, I've fallen in love with Iveta and that's why I'm taking any responsibility.
Worst female virtues: What's up with you?
Asking the men to name some typical female virtues, then invariably shake some out of their sleeves promptly.
Dear women, do you recognize yourself in the following lines, in which we review a few immoralities, who let the men want the blood in their veils?
shopping addiction
Does their husband accuse them of being shopping addicts?
Do you have to buy at least one quarrels weekly?
Do you like to go shopping and can it also be a bit more with promotions?
In your case, it’s really about a weakness.
Some women are at least aware of this and try to keep their shuffling halfway under control.
But hand on heart, which woman already manages to stroll through a clothes store in search of a well-fitting outerwear and not try everyone (in all possible color combinations) in the cabin?
Even if shopping is a hobby for most women, for men it's often pure hell.
Why don't they think about how many times they've told their husband before - you'd rather stay outside...
Continuing dissatisfaction
“I’m not too fat?”
"I'd have to lose at least five kilos - should I start jogging or doing gymnastics?"
"Do you even like me?"
Is it kind of familiar to them?
Yes?
Then I guess you're one of the women who's obsessed with how they look.
That doesn't mean you're supposed to let go, but many men are allergic to it when their wife constantly whines about their appearance.
The stronger sex agrees - with increasing frequency of complaints, women are increasingly incompatible.
Ordinance and cleanliness in the first place
It's a fight against windmills.
Cleaning windows, wiping tiles and dust, shuvering the tub at least twice a week.
If you scold with your partner, because he tramples on the clean tiles again with dirty shoes, scold the children, because the just chafed sink is dirty again and because the glass door on the living room closet already has fingerprints again, when polishing makes so much trouble?
If you suffer from this kind of "deviance", then you should know that you can't overdo anything and the order and cleanliness in family life don't come first.
Ultimately, this excessive purity can also harm the mutual relationships and, above all, rest in the family.
Stabbings
"Difficult sneakers come into the laundry basket."
“Do you really want to put on the old socks again tomorrow?”
"You don't just throw a wet towel on the floor."
If your partner is exposed to such a tirade, don’t be surprised that this puts him on.
Of course, that's not meant badly, they just want everything to have their order.
If the men knew this, then the women may not have had so much to complain about.
Gossip and gossip
Some women like to clap and gossip, there is scrambled or even slandered behind their backs or one forges covenants.
Women are focused on relationships, which is why they like to pane through such topics, such as - who, where, with whom, how and why.
Probably each of us women has a bit harmless gossip and gossip in stock.
Hand on heart - that's probably all women's own.
But this is not to be confused with gossies of the coarsest calibers, to whom nothing and no one is holy, who probably despise everyone in their environment and who pose a considerable danger especially for women's collectives.
