As a result of this victory, Philadelphia put itself at the helm of the eastern conference.
The Czech defender of Montreal Jaroslav Špaček was injured in the game against Buffalo and retired in the second third due to an injury to the upper body.
In addition to their experienced Beck, the Candiens also lost their lead an unlosted 2:3 in the penalty shoot-out.
